Printed with puzzle:
Hello? On the standard 22-Across telephone face (shown below), each of the numbers 2 through 9 appears with three letters of the alphabet. When you've come up with your answer to a clue, convert each of its letters to the appropriate number and enter the number in its proper square in the grid. Numbers in Across words do not necessarily represent the same letters in Down words. Get the message? Bye. (Click.)

